%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: b4b511b3ce7287f40bead898b1d8152f, type: 3}
  m_Name: Readme
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: BehaviorLLM.Editor::BehaviorLLM.Editor.Readme.BehaviorLLMReadme
  title: BehaviorLLM
  subtitle: 'Local-LLM decision making for Unity characters and game systems. Everything
    runs on this machine: no cloud API, no account, no per-call cost.'
  sections:
  - heading: What it does
    text: A Decision Maker senses the scene through observation modules, sends what
      it saw to a local language model, and gets back one action from a list you
      wrote. The model's reply is constrained to that list while it is being generated,
      so it cannot name an action that does not exist or an argument the action will
      not take. Each action is a UnityEvent, so the model chooses and your code executes.
    linkText: 
    linkTarget: 
  - heading: Getting a model running
    text: Open BehaviorLLM > Model Manager. Download one of the measured GGUF models
      in the Catalog tab, click Set active in current scene in the Installed tab, and
      install the inference server from the Server tab. The window writes into
      StreamingAssets and remembers what you chose. Nothing else in the package needs
      configuring before a character can think.
    linkText: 
    linkTarget: 
  - heading: The two samples
    text: 'StealthGuard is the one to read first: three guards patrol a compound,
      each with its own persona and patrol beat, all sharing one action set and one
      model. PrisonYard is the larger one: eight decision makers of three kinds,
      custom senses, and a warden that has no body at all and decides for the prison
      as a system.'
    linkText: Open the StealthGuard scene
    linkTarget: Samples/StealthGuard/Scenes/StealthGuard.unity
  - heading: Watching a decision happen
    text: 'BehaviorLLM > Prompt Inspector records every exchange between
      a decision maker and the model while the game runs: the prompt as it was sent,
      split into the half that is cached and the half that changes, the schema, and
      the reply. It is the fastest way to understand why a character chose what it
      chose.'
    linkText: 
    linkTarget: 
  - heading: What the samples need
    text: 'The package core has no package dependencies at all. The two samples do:
      AI Navigation for movement and the Input System for the player character. If
      either is missing the sample assemblies are skipped rather than broken, so
      the package still installs and works; install both from the Package Manager
      if you want to play them.'
    linkText: 
    linkTarget: 
  - heading: Documentation
    text: The package README covers installation and the first character end to end.
      The user guide under Documentation~ goes through observation modules, argument
      providers, decision profiles and the configuration assets.
    linkText: Open README.md
    linkTarget: README.md
  removableFolders:
  - displayName: StealthGuard sample
    folderPath: Samples/StealthGuard
    whatItCosts: The three-guard compound scene, its scripts and its art. Nothing
      else references it.
  - displayName: PrisonYard sample
    folderPath: Samples/PrisonYard
    whatItCosts: The eight-character prison scene, its scripts, its art and its editor
      tests. Nothing else references it.
  - displayName: Experiment data
    folderPath: Experiments~
    whatItCosts: The measurement harness and the recorded runs behind the numbers in
      the README. Unity never imports this folder; nothing references it.
